Staging evidence and remaining redistribution prerequisites:

The standalone source build writes erp/third-party-notices/index.json and
copies the full original texts beside it. Its lockfile/module/toolchain
provenance and per-text SHA-256 make the collection inspectable. The platform
assemblers verify those bytes and the existing Node/Auth/PostgREST/Ollama/
PostgreSQL license files before finishing. No runtime notice fetch occurs.
Collection logs every missing full text; strict `audit`/`bundle` modes refuse
unresolved entries rather than treating SPDX metadata or URLs as permission.

Known upstream gaps found during source inspection: maath 0.10.8 and stats-gl
2.4.2 omit full license texts both in their installed packages and in the
inspected version-tag/gitHead source trees. MediaPipe tasks-vision 0.10.17
omits a full license file; original declaration copyright headers are preserved,
but they do not establish the complete bundled WASM third-party notice closure.
These are findings about potential source packages,
not proof each optional component survived the client build. They become release
blockers only when their code or files are in the actual staged/server or emitted
client-module set. Resolve exact original texts/notices for any such actual
component before publishing; do not fabricate notices from author fields, assume
a nearby version, or silently waive the gate.

